          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_ROLLING_KINEMATICS_ENERGY",
          "title": "1. Pure Rolling Kinematics and Kinetic Energy",
          "contentMarkdown": "In pure rolling without slipping, contact point speed is zero and $$v_{\\\\text{cm}} = R\\\\omega$$. Rotational kinetic energy is $$K_{\\\\text{rot}} = \\\\frac{1}{2}I\\\\omega^2$$ and total kinetic energy is $$K_{\\\\text{total}} = \\\\frac{1}{2} M v_{\\\\text{cm}}^2 \\\\left[1 + \\\\frac{k^2}{R^2}\\\\right]$$.",
