        },
        {
          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_1C4E0301_CONCEPTS_02_INCLINED_PLANE_ROLLING",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR_INCLINED_PLANE_ROLLING",
          "title": "2. Acceleration Rolling Down an Inclined Plane",
          "contentMarkdown": "Linear acceleration rolling down an incline of angle $\\\\theta$ is $$a_{\\\\text{cm}} = \\\\frac{g\\\\sin\\\\theta}{1 + k^2/R^2}$$. A solid sphere reaches bottom first because its $k^2/R^2 = 2/5$ is lowest.",
